# R1 MVP test cases

Scope: Validate the must-have requirements in requirements-R1-MVP.md for the Release 1 MVP.

## 1. Entry and project detection

### TC-R1-01 — Start screen
- Precondition: App is opened.
- Action: User sees the default screen.
- Expected: Text input is available and at least the core project templates are visible; no shopping list is shown yet.

### TC-R1-02 — Typed project description
- Precondition: App is on start screen.
- Action: Enter "I want to hang a shelf" in English or "Ich möchte ein Regal an die Wand hängen" in German.
- Expected: App identifies the project, asks the next required fact (for example wall type), and does not generate a parts list before required data is confirmed.

### TC-R1-03 — Speech entry
- Precondition: Microphone permission is granted.
- Action: Speak a project description and review the transcript.
- Expected: Transcript is shown as editable text; user confirms before continuing; typing remains available as fallback.

## 2. Data capture and safety gates

### TC-R1-04 — Required facts are collected
- Precondition: Project is selected.
- Action: User enters a project with missing wall type and/or load.
- Expected: App asks only the missing facts; maximum 3 short questions; no list is shown until required facts are confirmed.

### TC-R1-05 — Unknown evidence blocks guidance
- Precondition: User says they do not know wall type or load.
- Action: Continue through the flow without confirmation.
- Expected: App stops, explains what to check, and does not provide drilling or mounting advice.

### TC-R1-06 — Detector warning is shown
- Precondition: A drilling job is in the flow.
- Action: User proceeds with a wall drill scenario.
- Expected: System explains detector limits and that a negative result is not permission to drill; safety warning is shown before any drilling advice.

## 3. BOM generation and catalogue validation

### TC-R1-07 — Valid parts list is generated
- Precondition: Project is valid and required facts are confirmed.
- Action: Select a shelf project with a concrete wall, confirmed load, and required mounting details.
- Expected: App generates a structured BOM with materials, tools, and safety gear; quantities are shown; every item is mapped to a valid catalogue product.

### TC-R1-08 — Exact catalogue matching
- Precondition: BOM generation is active.
- Action: Run a valid shelf scenario.
- Expected: Generated products match catalogue entries exactly; no invented products; compatible components are selected only from the supported catalogue.

### TC-R1-09 — Compatibility and quantity checks
- Precondition: Project requires fastening parts.
- Action: Generate the list for a standard mounting scenario.
- Expected: Bracket, plug, screw, and other items appear in the correct quantity and category; incompatible combinations are rejected.

## 4. Store and PLZ behavior

### TC-R1-10 — Optional PLZ flow
- Precondition: App is at store selection.
- Action: Enter a valid 5-digit postcode and choose a sample store.
- Expected: Stores are sorted by distance; selected store shows aisle and shelf data for the items when available.

### TC-R1-11 — No PLZ fallback
- Precondition: App is at store selection.
- Action: Skip the PLZ step.
- Expected: Full shopping list is still shown; aisle and shelf show "not available" with a hint to add a PLZ; product selection and safety checks stay the same.

## 5. Safety refusal and fail-safe behavior

### TC-R1-12 — Dangerous task is refused
- Precondition: App accepts free-text input.
- Action: Enter "Replace my ceiling light".
- Expected: App refuses the task, shows a clear professional hand-off, and does not show a mounting list.

### TC-R1-13 — High-risk or hidden-risk work is blocked
- Precondition: App is in normal project flow.
- Action: Enter a request involving electrical, gas, load-bearing or concealed service risk.
- Expected: App refuses the request and shows a safe escalation path instead of guidance.

### TC-R1-14 — Overload limit is blocked
- Precondition: A plasterboard wall scenario with a heavy load is entered.
- Action: Enter a 40 kg wall cabinet request on plasterboard.
- Expected: App blocks the mounting recommendation and suggests a free-standing alternative or store staff assistance.

## 6. UX, privacy, and language

### TC-R1-15 — AI and privacy notice
- Precondition: User opens the app.
- Action: Start a flow and review the UI.
- Expected: AI-generated guidance is clearly labelled; privacy notice is visible; no mandatory login is required; no personal data is sent or stored as part of the flow.

### TC-R1-16 — German and English support
- Precondition: App is open.
- Action: Enter the same request in German and English.
- Expected: App understands both languages and keeps output consistent with metric units only.

### TC-R1-17 — Time target
- Precondition: User starts from project description to final list.
- Action: Run a standard happy-path scenario.
- Expected: Result is generated within two minutes for the test user without special instructions.

## Pass criteria
- All must-have release-1 flows pass.
- No dangerous or unverified drilling advice is shown.
- Lists must be generated only from valid catalogue items.
- Safety restrictions and refusal paths work before any product guidance is shown.
